  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc. The dominant finding is that RNA with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool is the strongest single-modality configuration, and image-only (ResNet50) was very weak (0.208). The key remaining question is whether adding the image modality via fusion to the best RNA configuration can push accuracy above 0.650. Config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the minimal, logical extension of the best RNA setup: it keeps the proven multiprofile + scvi_n200 + avgpool settings and adds ResNet50 image features with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion without simultaneously changing aggregation or fusion strategy. If it improves, remaining budget can explore weighted fusion or ViT; if it doesn't, it confirms RNA-only is optimal and we can exploit further. This is the highest-information experiment under the 3-experiment remaining budget."
}

